A long time ago, Malcolm Ryan made a patch to display statues in tty
mode as the letter of the monster instead of a backtick.   I really
liked that patch.  The biggest problem was that it changed the save
files, because it made a new glyph for each possible type of statue.

Here is an improved shorter patch that achieves the same effect.  This
patch uses the ``drawing'' system (mapglyph.c) to replace the backticks
with letters.  As you can see, there are no save file changes.

This new patch doesn't implement as many YANMs as the old patch.  Also,
the bug on line 1555 of zap.c is not fixed, although the old patch
fixed it.  These features of the old patch could be added without
breaking save files, but I want to start with something simple to see
what people think about it.

The patch is just the addition of three lines in mapglyph.c.

